# Commit separation: ddai-artifacts/ vs projects/

NEVER stage or commit files under `ddai-artifacts/` together with files under
`projects/` in the same git commit. These two trees must always go into separate
commits.

When a change touches both trees:

1. Stage and commit the `projects/` files in one commit.
2. Stage and commit the `ddai-artifacts/` files in a separate commit.

The order between the two is not important, but they must never share a commit.

Example (two changed files, one in each tree):

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — two separate commits
git add projects/rccl-tests/src/reduce_scatter.cu
git commit -m "rccl-tests: ..."
git add ddai-artifacts/scripts/gin-sdma-reducescatter-test.bash
git commit -m "artifacts: ..."

# ❌ BAD — both trees in one commit
git add projects/... ddai-artifacts/...
git commit -m "..."
```

When using `git commit -a` or `git add -A`/`git add .`, check `git status`
first and stage each tree explicitly so the two never end up in one commit.
